WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.200
- Well, I have to ask,

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.263
did any of the coaches try to
take advantage of my absence?

00:00:06.127 --> 00:00:09.320
- (laughs) I mean, their
biggest thing was they refused

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:10.950
to admit that you didn't feel good,

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.870
they were like, "She's on a beach.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.030
She needs a break.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.860
I was like 18 jobs.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:17.700
She wanted a tan. She's gone."

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:18.877
And I was like

00:00:18.877 --> 00:00:21.710
"I'm sure she'd rather be
doing that than being sick."

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:25.210
But other than that, they, they love you.

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:26.190
They really love you.

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:29.050
So they didn't talk any
crap at all. (laughs)

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:31.800
- Oh man, I bet that all
came from Shelton too.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.260
Um, we, I was not on vacation.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.980
I was in hell with a sinus infection

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.510
but we were in constant
contact though all weekend.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.000
I think people are
probably going to see you

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.610
on your phone a lot and think
you're just like texting

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:43.710
like your friends or something.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.450
But we were texting the
entire time on this show

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:47.770
and I don't know if you know

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.170
people are going to know that or not

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.003
so I wanted to say that

00:00:50.003 --> 00:00:52.550
but did I help you or
hurt you by doing that?

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.670
- Oh God, I, you helped me so much.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:56.470
And for reference, for everyone listening

00:00:56.470 --> 00:01:01.470
like Kelly called me at
7:00 PM Nashville time.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.700
And they were shooting the
next day at 1:00 PM in LA.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.340
And, and so I

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:10.110
I fully went back to college,
like on the flight over

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:11.990
she sent me all of the blind auditions,

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:15.490
she sent me everything about
like everyone on her team,

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:17.060
what she loved, what she was looking for,

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.350
and so as soon as I landed you and I got

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:22.060
to talk and you just like downloaded all

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.187
of your incredible
knowledge and you were like

00:01:24.187 --> 00:01:25.610
"This is what I love about this person.

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:26.630
This is what I want to see."

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:29.327
And so when I got in
the chair, I was like,

00:01:29.327 --> 00:01:30.870
"First of all where's that seat warmer

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:32.450
that you were telling me
about because it is cold."

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:33.680
- [Kelly] I, I told you!

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:35.250
I was like, "Look for the seat warmer.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.090
Your butt is going to be so cold."

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:39.100
And I wear Spanx girl, I'm all covered up

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.070
but I understand it's you.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:42.700
I'm cold! You had to be dying.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.870
But can you, can you tell everyone like

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:45.940
about this week's episode?

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:46.773
Cause I wasn't there.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:47.690
So you would know.

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:51.000
- Honestly, it's, it's so
crazy because obviously

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.570
there's great talent on a
show called "The Voice".

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:53.570
Like the voices are crazy

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:54.950
but when you're actually sitting there

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:58.480
in the room and you're
watching these, these artists

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.380
some of them are like really seasoned

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:02.220
and then some of them are really early on

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.520
in like discovering their instrument.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:08.350
You're watching them, just,
I just had goosebumps most

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:11.620
of the time, just the talent
is really crazy this season.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:15.910
Um, and the one thing you asked
me was to keep the rivalry

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:16.743
with Blake,

00:02:16.743 --> 00:02:18.580
and so I really took that to heart.

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:20.870
So those are the two
things that I can tell you

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:22.272
is that the talent's really great,

00:02:22.272 --> 00:02:24.560
the choices were really hard,

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.070
but we talked about it and Blake
probably hates me. (laughs)

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:28.960
- Oh my God.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:31.280
I was so excited about the dad thing.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:32.540
I can't even tell you.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:35.237
I was like, "Oh my God,
she's my favorite."

